    <dashboard name='Story 1' type='storyboard'>
      <style>
        <style-rule element='story-point-caption'>
          <format attr='width' value='291' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size maxheight='964' maxwidth='1016' minheight='964' minwidth='1016' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98340' id='1' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98426' x='787' y='830'>
            <zone h='4357' id='3' type-v2='title' w='98426' x='787' y='830' />
            <zone h='10477' id='4' is-fixed='true' paired-zone-id='5' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='98426' x='787' y='5187' />
            <zone h='83506' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='98426' x='787' y='15664'>
              <flipboard active-id='2' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                <story-points>
                  <story-point caption='**Introduction: Global Fuel Prices &amp; Taxation Trends**&#10;&#10;This project analyzes global fuel prices and taxation patterns across 84 countries from January 2020 to April 2026. It explores regional price differences, changes in fuel prices over time, and the relationship between fuel prices, taxation, income levels, and subsidies.&#10;' captured-sheet='GLOBAL FUEL PRICES &amp; TAXATION TRENDS (2020-2026)' id='1' />
                  <story-point caption='**Geographic Disparity: Global Fuel Price Distribution**&#10;&#10;This scene compares petrol and diesel prices across countries to explore geographical differences in fuel pricing. These variations may be associated with taxation, subsidies, and country-specific market conditions.&#10;' captured-sheet='Dashboard 2' id='2' />
                  <story-point caption='**Temporal Trends: Global Fuel Prices (2020–2026)**&#10;&#10;This scene examines changes in petrol, diesel, LPG, and Brent crude prices over time. Comparing these trends helps identify price movements and differences between fuel categories from January 2020 to April 2026.&#10;' captured-sheet='Dashboard 3' id='3' />
                  <story-point caption='Taxation Policy: Global Fuel Tax Comparison&#10;&#10;This scene compares average fuel tax percentages across regions and identifies countries with higher average tax rates. It also explores differences in fuel prices among selected countries. These comparisons reveal patterns and associations but do not prove that taxation alone causes higher or lower fuel prices.&#10;' captured-sheet='Dashboard 4' id='4' />
                  <story-point caption='Economic Impact: Fuel Prices by Income Level&#10;&#10;This scene compares average petrol prices across income-level categories. It explores whether fuel prices differ between economic groups. Income level alone does not establish the cause of price differences; taxation, subsidies, and other country-specific factors may also contribute.&#10;&#10;&#10;This scene compares average petrol prices across income-level categories. It explores whether fuel prices differ between economic groups. Income level alone does not establish the cause of price differences; taxation, subsidies, and other country-specific factors may also contribute.&#10;' captured-sheet='Fuel Prices by Income Level' id='5'>
                    <capturedDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='Fuel Prices by Income Level'>
                        <shelf-sort-deltas>
                          <clear-shelf-sorts>
                            <clear-shelf-sort-v2 dimension='[federated.1ezdb5d1vxnchl1gsjruq10bt6ja].[none:income_level:nk]' is-on-innermost-dimension='true' shelf='rows' />
                          </clear-shelf-sorts>
                        </shelf-sort-deltas>
                      </worksheet>
                    </capturedDeltas>
                  </story-point>
                  <story-point caption='**Subsidy Assessment: Government Support and Fuel Prices**&#10;&#10;This scene compares average petrol prices across subsidy-level categories. It explores whether fuel prices vary with the recorded level of government support. These comparisons reveal patterns in the dataset but do not, by themselves, prove that subsidies directly cause lower or higher fuel prices.&#10;' captured-sheet='Fuel Prices by Subsidy Level' id='6' />
                  <story-point caption='Conclusions &amp; Recommendations&#10;&#10;This project compares global fuel prices, taxation, and regional differences across 84 countries. The analysis helps identify variations in fuel prices and supports further investigation into taxation, income levels, and subsidy policies. Policymakers should consider country-specific economic conditions before drawing conclusions or making policy decisions.&#10;' captured-sheet='Sheet 16' id='7' />
                </story-points>
              </flipboard>
            </zone>
          </zone>
